# Browser
# A cloaked card with morph can be turned face up two ways (CR 701.58c, 702.37e): for its mana cost, as any cloaked creature
# card, or for its morph cost. Cryptic Coat cloaks Branchsnap Lorian from the top of Bot1's library; Bot1's page offers the
# face-down permanent both, each row naming its own cost - "Turn face up — Morph {G}" and "Turn face up for its mana cost" - and
# Bot1 turns it up for {G} with Mox Emerald. Face up it is Branchsnap Lorian, a 4/1 with trample, and the Coat's +1/+0.

